            <ArticleTitle>Total synthesis and stereochemical determination of yoshinone A.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>109-114</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0031-9422(16)30217-5</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.phytochem.2016.10.005</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>In 2014, the γ-pyrone-containing polyketide, yoshinone A, was isolated from the marine cyanobacterium Leptolyngbya sp. and its structure was determined. Yoshinone A inhibited differentiation of 3T3-L1 cells into adipocytes, with an EC50 value of 420 nM without any cytotoxicity, and therefore is expected to be a lead compound for obesity drugs. To establish its absolute configuration, and to provide sufficient amounts for further research, the total synthesis of yoshinone A was achieved through synthesis of its two possible diastereomers.</AbstractText>
